{
  "additional_concerns": [
    "The aggregate-exposure input delegates identification, valuation, look-through and aggregation to an unspecified methodology. The formula preserves the threshold structure but does not establish measurement correctness.",
    "The source's indirect-exposure examples are expressly non-exhaustive and subject to SFC updates. An upstream implementation must not treat BDCs, CLOs, TRSs and SRTs as a closed list.",
    "Footnote 1 states a separate 15% direct-investment limit under UT Code 7.3. The classification formula neither tests that limit nor authorizes exposures exceeding it; classification must not be read as investment-limit compliance.",
    "The global conflict-blocking rule can prevent a classification result even when the other disjunct independently establishes the trigger. This is a declared evidence-handling restriction, not a condition imposed by the circular.",
    "The supplied missing dependency IDs have no authority titles or mappings. None can reliably be assigned to a named external authority.",
    "The retained text supplies no commencement date or transition period. Assessment-time applicability and any designation's operative status require evidence; prompt document updates do not create a classification grace period."
  ],
